      "set-cell"
    ],
    "solution_steps": [
      "find the first color-4 marker in row-major order",
      "round its row and column down to multiples of four to locate the source 3x3 interior",
      "multiply its local row and column within that interior by four to locate the destination interior",
      "collect source-interior cells whose values are neither zero nor gray 5, including the marker",
      "construct a base output that preserves every gray-5 cell and clears every other cell to zero",
      "copy each collected source value to the same local offset in the destination interior"
    ],
    "source": "canonical program and reviewed semantic audit",
    "target_status": "reviewed_semantic_description",
    "target_text": "Use the first yellow marker's quotient coordinates as the source 3x3 macro-cell and its local coordinates as the destination macro-cell; preserve gray, clear everything else, then copy every nonzero/non-gray source cell\u2014including the marker\u2014to the destination at the same offset."
